# Auto-Reply System Upgrade Plan

## Goal Description
Upgrade the current simple "Keyword -> Reply" system to a "Pro" rule engine. This includes adding support for Regex matching, Custom Sender Identities (override bot name/icon), Flex Messages (JSON payload), Quick Replies, and automatic Tag assignment.

## User Review Required
> [!IMPORTANT]
> The default `matchType` for new keywords will be changed to `EXACT` (currently schema says `CONTAINS`, but code defaults to `EXACT` in [keyword-settings.tsx](file:///d:/Workshop/line_oa/admin_panel/src/components/automation/keyword-settings.tsx)).
> I will update the schema default to `EXACT` as requested.

## Proposed Changes

### Database Schema
#### [MODIFY] [schema.prisma](file:///d:/Workshop/line_oa/admin_panel/prisma/schema.prisma)
- Update `AutoReplyKeyword` model:
    - Change `matchType` default to `EXACT`.
    - Add `description` (String?).
    - Add `senderName` (String?).
    - Add `senderIconUrl` (String?).
    - Add `quickReplies` (Json?).
    - Add `tagsToAdd` (String[]).

### UI Components
#### [MODIFY] [keyword-settings.tsx](file:///d:/Workshop/line_oa/admin_panel/src/components/automation/keyword-settings.tsx)
- Redesign the "Add/Edit Rule" Dialog with a Tabbed or Accordion interface.
- **Trigger Tab**: Keyword, Match Type (Exact/Regex), Description.
- **Reply Tab**:
    - Reply Type Selector (Text / Flex).
    - Content Editor (Textarea for Text, JSON Editor for Flex).
    - Sender Identity (Name, Icon).
    - Quick Replies Builder (Dynamic list of buttons).
- **Actions Tab**:
    - Tags input (Add tags to user on match).

### Backend Logic
#### [MODIFY] [route.ts](file:///d:/Workshop/line_oa/admin_panel/src/app/api/webhook/line/route.ts)
- Refactor [handleMessageEvent](file:///d:/Workshop/line_oa/admin_panel/src/app/api/webhook/line/route.ts#137-285) to support complex matching.
- **Matching Logic**:
    - Fetch active rules.
    - Iterate to check `EXACT` matches first, then `REGEX`.
    - Use `new RegExp(keyword).test(userMessage)` for regex type.
- **Execution Logic**:
    - If match found:
        - Construct message payload (TEXT or FLEX).
        - append `sender` and `quickReply` objects if present.
        - Send reply via `lineClient`.
        - Apply `tagsToAdd` to the `Customer` record.

## Verification Plan

### Automated Tests
- None existing for UI interactions.

### Manual Verification
1.  **Database Migration**: Run `npx prisma migrate dev` and verify no errors.
2.  **UI Testing**:
    - Open Automation > Auto-Reply.
    - Create a rule with **Regex** (e.g., `^hello.*`).
    - Set a **Custom Sender** (e.g., "Support Bot").
    - Add a **Quick Reply** button.
    - Add a **Tag** to apply (e.g., "Tested").
3.  **Functional Testing** (requires LINE App):
    - Send "hello world" to the bot.
    - Verify:
        - Bot replies with custom sender name/icon.
        - Quick reply buttons appear.
        - Admin Panel > Users tag list includes "Tested".
